I've left out the `http-client` import and the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause is stated as its entire authority, so adding that grant would contradict the contract. The fetch would also send the raw untrusted message text, unencoded, to an external host, and its result never affects the output. That makes it an outbound data channel rather than enrichment. If the platform team has approved the grant, the `with` clause and graph contract need updating first. The URL should also percent-encode the query and send only the minimum necessary text. I can add it once those are settled.

